            type: "list",
            items: [
              "Trauma reactions are real and vary widely; having them does not indicate weakness.",
              "Most people exposed to a potentially traumatic event do not develop PTSD.",
              "PTSD can be assessed and treated; recovery is possible.",
              "Safety and voluntary choice come before exercises or detailed storytelling.",
              "Grounding and routines are optional coping supports, not substitutes for trauma-focused therapy.",
              "Seek professional assessment for severe, persistent or disabling symptoms.",
            ],
